To find the angle a **space diagonal** makes with the base, work in the triangle formed by the **base diagonal** and the vertical height.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (B2) at (6.752,1.3);
\coordinate (A2) at (2.252,1.3);
\coordinate (At) at (0,3.5);
\coordinate (Bt) at (4.5,3.5);
\coordinate (B2t) at (6.752,4.8);
\coordinate (A2t) at (2.252,4.8);
\fill[blue!12] (A)--(B2)--(B2t)--cycle;
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(B2);
\draw (A)--(At);
\draw (B)--(Bt);
\draw (B2)--(B2t) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\draw (At)--(Bt)--(B2t)--(A2t)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A)--(A2);
\draw[dashed] (A2)--(B2);
\draw[dashed] (A2)--(A2t);
\draw[blue,dashed] (A)--(B2);
\draw[red,thick] (A)--(B2t);
\coordinate (sa) at ($(B2)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (sb) at ($(B2)!0.3cm!(B2t)$);
\draw (sa)--($(sa)+(sb)-(B2)$)--(sb);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=1.4cm,angle eccentricity=1.45] {angle=B2--A--B2t};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For a **square pyramid whose apex lies vertically above the centre of the square base**, the angle a **side face** makes with the base uses half a base side as the horizontal leg.

[tikz]

\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles,quotes}
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings,
  mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.602,1.5);
\coordinate (D) at (-2.598,1.5);
\coordinate (O) at (1.301,0.75);
\coordinate (T) at (1.301,4.35);
\coordinate (M) at (2.6,0);
\fill[blue!12] (T)--(O)--(M)--cycle;
\draw[tickmark] (A)--(M);
\draw[tickmark] (M)--(B);
\draw (A)--(D);
\draw[dashed] (D)--(C);
\draw[dashed] (C)--(B);
\draw (T)--(A);
\draw (T)--(B);
\draw (T)--(D);
\draw[dashed] (T)--(C);
\draw[blue,dashed] (O)--(T);
\draw[blue,dashed] (O)--(M);
\draw[blue,thick] (M)--(T);
\coordinate (ra) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(M)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(T)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(O)$)--(rb);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.75cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=T--M--O};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For a **square pyramid whose apex lies vertically above the centre of the square base**, the angle a **slant edge** makes with the base instead uses half the base diagonal, with the perpendicular height as the vertical leg.

[tikz]

\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc,angles,quotes}
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{tickmark/.style={postaction={decorate, decoration={markings,
  mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw[black] (0pt,-4pt) -- (0pt,4pt);}}}}}\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.602,1.5);
\coordinate (D) at (-2.598,1.5);
\coordinate (O) at (1.301,0.75);
\coordinate (T) at (1.301,4.35);
\fill[blue!12] (A)--(O)--(T)--cycle;
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (A)--(D);
\draw[dashed] (D)--(C);
\draw[dashed] (C)--(B);
\draw (T)--(B);
\draw (T)--(D);
\draw[dashed] (T)--(C);
\draw[blue,thick] (T)--(A);
\draw[blue,dashed] (O)--(T);
\draw[blue,tickmark] (A)--(O);
\draw[blue,dashed,tickmark] (O)--(C);
\coordinate (ra) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(T)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(O)$)--(rb);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=1.0cm,angle eccentricity=1.55] {angle=C--A--T};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Because **due south** and **due east** are perpendicular, the two ground distances and the line joining the endpoints form a right-angled triangle.

[tikz]
