\coordinate (rqa) at ($(Rt)!0.26cm!(L)$);
\coordinate (rqb) at ($(Rt)!0.26cm!(Tp)$);
\draw (rqa)--($(rqa)+(rqb)-(Rt)$)--(rqb);
\draw (L)--(Rt) node[midway,below] {$BQ$};
\draw (Rt)--(Tp) node[midway,right] {$h$};
\draw (L)--(Tp) node[midway,above left] {$QT$};
\pic[draw,"$30^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.35] {angle=Rt--L--Tp};
\node[below left] at (L) {$Q$};
\node[below right] at (Rt) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (Tp) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In the top-down right-angled triangle $PBQ$ (right angle at $B$), $BQ$ is opposite the $040^{\circ}$ angle at $P$.
$BQ=60\sin40^{\circ}$
$=38.56\ldots\text{ m}$
Now use the elevation from $Q$.
$\tan30^{\circ}=\dfrac{h}{38.56\ldots}$
$h=38.56\ldots\times\tan30^{\circ}$
$\approx22\text{ m}$

