From point $A$ the tower at $O$ is on a bearing of $300^{\circ}$T; from point $B$ it is on a bearing of $030^{\circ}$T. The tower is $90$ m tall.
The angle of elevation of the top from $A$ is $25^{\circ}$ and from $B$ is $40^{\circ}$.
Find the distance $AB$, to the nearest metre.

development.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-3.000,0);
\coordinate (B) at (0,1.667);
\draw (A)--(C)--(B)--cycle;
\coordinate (ra) at ($(C)!0.26cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(C)!0.26cm!(B)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(C)$)--(rb);
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$OA$};
\draw (C)--(B) node[midway,right] {$OB$};
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$AB$};
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Reverse bearings differ by $180^{\circ}$. From $O$, the bearing of $A$ is $300^{\circ}-180^{\circ}=120^{\circ}$ and the bearing of $B$ is $30^{\circ}+180^{\circ}=210^{\circ}$.
The angle at $O$ is $210^{\circ}-120^{\circ}=90^{\circ}$, so $\triangle OAB$ is right-angled at $O$.
$OA=\dfrac{90}{\tan25^{\circ}}$
$=193.00\ldots\text{ m}$
$OB=\dfrac{90}{\tan40^{\circ}}$
$=107.25\ldots\text{ m}$
$AB=\sqrt{OA^2+OB^2}$
$=\sqrt{193.00\ldots^2+107.25\ldots^2}$
$\approx221\text{ m}$

