A lighthouse $LO$ is $200$ m above sea level.
From boat $A$ the bearing of the lighthouse is $035^{\circ}$T and its angle of depression from the top is $14^{\circ}$; from boat $B$ the bearing of the lighthouse is $305^{\circ}$T and its angle of depression is $19^{\circ}$.
Find the distance $AB$ between the boats, to the nearest metre.

mastery.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-3.000,0);
\coordinate (B) at (0,2.172);
\draw (A)--(C)--(B)--cycle;
\coordinate (ra) at ($(C)!0.26cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (rb) at ($(C)!0.26cm!(B)$);
\draw (ra)--($(ra)+(rb)-(C)$)--(rb);
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,below] {$OA$};
\draw (C)--(B) node[midway,right] {$OB$};
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above left] {$AB$};
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Each angle of depression equals the angle of elevation of the lighthouse from that boat.
Drawing the top-down view, the reverse bearings from $O$ to $A$ and $B$ are $215^{\circ}$T and $125^{\circ}$T, so the angle at $O$ is $215^{\circ}-125^{\circ}=90^{\circ}$.
$OA=\dfrac{200}{\tan14^{\circ}}$
$=802.15\ldots\text{ m}$
$OB=\dfrac{200}{\tan19^{\circ}}$
$=580.84\ldots\text{ m}$
$AB=\sqrt{OA^2+OB^2}$
$=\sqrt{802.15\ldots^2+580.84\ldots^2}$
$\approx990\text{ m}$

